    "name": "Trumped Iris Rhizome (Bulb)",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">The 'Trumped' iris is a&nbsp;Tall Bearded iris, introduced by Tom Burseen in 2008, featuring white standards with yellow bases, ruffled plum purple falls with washed edges and strong bronze hafts, and fat, bronze beards.&nbsp;It grows to about 35 inches tall, blooms mid to late season, and is known for its unique coloring and ruffled petals.&nbsp;</span></p>",
